Are you sure?

371
00:17:21,050 --> 00:17:22,970
- Yeah. - Okay.

372
00:17:23,050 --> 00:17:24,100
Howard come back.

373
00:17:24,190 --> 00:17:26,520
Oh, you guys had me scared for a minute.

374
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:30,700
No, no, no, no!

375
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:33,300
That rate is much too low from what we'd expect from this collision.

376
00:17:33,370 --> 00:17:34,550
Do you understand

377
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:37,340
We're talking about Dark Matter colliding in outer space?

378
00:17:37,420 --> 00:17:38,750
Of course I understand.

379
00:17:38,820 --> 00:17:41,120
And who are you to tell me about outer space?

380
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:42,340
I'm the astrophysicist.

381
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:43,840
"astro" means "space"

382
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:47,030
"astro" means "star"

383
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,050
Okay, well, let me just tell you,

384
00:17:49,130 --> 00:17:51,380
If we having this argument in my native language

385
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:53,630
I'd be kicking your butt.

386
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:57,120
English is your native language.

387
00:17:57,190 --> 00:18:01,640
Okay, you got me there, but you're wrong about this!

388
00:18:01,690 --> 00:18:03,860
There is a fine line between wrong and visionary.

389
00:18:03,950 --> 00:18:06,360
Unfortunately you have to be a visionary to see it.

390
00:18:07,030 --> 00:18:09,850
My god, you think that every thought

391
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:11,720
